WEBVTT

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.380
There are guys out there who are

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:10.260
I want to become a manga
editor no matter what!!

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.280
just like those prince-like
dudes in shojo manga.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.940
They're surrounded by sparkles and flowers.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.740
That book I bought the last time was so good.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.260
Of course it was.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.570
I had recommended it after all.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.420
I hate these flashy guys,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.010
and yet...

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.020
And yet I love...

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.530
...his face.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.540
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.540
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.090
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.090
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.720
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.720
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.510
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.510
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.520
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.520
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.350
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.350
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:32.730
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:32.730
If I reach out my hand

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.110
hajimete no kimochi

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.110
Will you understand my feelings?

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.490
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.490
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.870
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.870
I love you more and more every second

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:50.000
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:50.000
We're still far from a happy ending

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:58.970
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:58.970
But I want to make it come true

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.430
tsuzuite yuku

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.430
Our story continues

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:17.400
Shouta Kisa, one of the editors for
Marukawa Publishing's Monthly Emerald.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:22.760
For some reason, he's only been
drawn to men his whole life.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.330
And he's a total sucker for good looks.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.240
So, what?

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.900
I know that a short, old man
who's into beautiful guys...

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.080
...can't expect to experience real romance.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.190
That's why I'm only looking.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.890
Boss, I really think you ought
to give Yukina a warning!

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.140
All he does all day is flirt
and talk with the girls!

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.700
Didn't you know?

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.150
That's his sales ploy.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.150
Here's my list of recommendations for today!

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.150
The titles coming out this week are...

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.280
...this, this and this.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.160
"Girl's Master" is a must-read!

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.160
That's the book I was in charge of...

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.750
I've been following this series
since it was still in the magazines,

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.630
but I could really empathize
with the main character.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.300
The story is standard,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.980
but there's plenty of bite and I thought
the male characters were really cool.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.150
So, is it good?

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.890
I thought it was great!

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.240
And then...

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.370
So he's been following it
since it was serialized.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.600
I guess it's not weird
for him to read them...

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.580
...if he's responsible for the
shojo manga section here.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.160
I suppose I kind of like that.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.600
Aw, man, what am I going to do?

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:42.950
My phone bill this month is huge.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.390
That's too bad.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.670
I was really hoping you could...

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:50.080
...read it quickly, so we could
bond over how good it is.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.040
I'm getting it!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:53.640
Me, too!

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:54.580
And me!

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.370
But how come you're selling
shojo manga, Yukina?

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.340
Well, that's easy.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.970
Working here means I get to see you guys.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.970
Is he a host or what?

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.890
Thanks and come again!

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.020
We will!

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.170
Uh, I am grateful that he's
selling my books, but...

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.990
I saw his name on his name tag.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:26.470
Marimo Books
Yukina

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.490
But I still don't know
what his first name is.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.390
On the way home,

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.460
I had randomly stopped in a bookstore and...

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.340
...he wound up being my cashier.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.000
Would you like me to cover the book for you?

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:38.500
No thanks.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.120
Damn!

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.510
This would have been the perfect
excuse to linger a bit longer!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.010
It was love at first sight.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.010
But we have no connection,

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.800
beyond that of a customer and a cashier.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.340
In any case, I really need to stop...

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:59.020
...falling in love with
people based on looks alone.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.850
But what can I do when he's perfect?

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.450
He's ideal,

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.990
especially his eyes and his face.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.310
His nose, his eyebrows, his mouth...

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.540
All of him.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.980
And he's tall.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.830
He had a nice body... too.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.090
If I had to name a fault,
it would be his personality.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.550
Our personalities would definitely
clash if we actually went out.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.050
Not that we ever could go out anyway!

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:37.460
Love at first sight works
well enough in a manga,

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.190
but this is reality.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.190
Good morning!

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.700
I've got to check the sales
stats for the new book.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.330
I guess it's not horrible,
but it's not great either.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.720
This isn't enough to compete with the
editor-in-chief's book coming out today,

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.790
not by a long shot.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.700
To be honest,

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:07.260
I'd really like to take one of
my projects to the next level.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.720
Actually, I need to do that for my career.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.700
Girl's Master

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.490
And I'm not getting any younger.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.360
I did have a hit project in the past,

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.250
but right before things could take off,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:26.260
the author got married and retired.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:35.240
Well, there's nothing more
important than their happiness...

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.450
Rit, what's all this?!

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.130
The storyboards for all of our
magazines published in the last five years.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.870
What are you doing with those?

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.110
The editor-in-chief told me to go through
each one from beginning to end,

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:52.090
and make sure I can explain how
and why each correction was added.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.640
And you're really going to do
it all for the storyboards?

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.800
That's impossible.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:58.650
You're the one who told me to do it,

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.930
and I said I would, so I will!

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.130
Well, good luck, rookie editor.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.650
Thank you!

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:13.660
Oh yeah, there was a time when
I was all gung-ho about work, too.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.770
Where does that random enthusiasm come from?

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:27.460
But then, as my career progressed,

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.180
and I got to know more and more
people from this industry,

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.750
I realized that I was a normal person.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.900
It's not that I can't do my job,

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.780
but I'm not anything special either.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:48.690
A person you would call special is
someone like our editor-in-chief, Takano.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.600
One day, we suddenly had a new editor-in-chief.

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:55.700
He took this dying magazine and
built it back up in just a year.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.500
Everything he does is crazy,

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.180
but the reason everyone goes with it is...

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:04.840
...because he really delivers
undeniably good results.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.810
I guess by now,

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:10.290
everyone is doing the best that they can.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:15.630
I suppose I'm not doing too bad compared
to everyone else in the company,

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.220
but the position I'm in has a
very high level of competency.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:26.710
The only certain thing is that I won't
ever be someone like the editor-in-chief.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.170
It's not like I'm feeling
depressed or anything,

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:32.190
I'm just being realistic.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.780
But I wouldn't mind being at
the helm of a popular project.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.220
Girl's Master

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:44.500
I keep thinking that I could never do it,

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.210
but I like this job enough to stay.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:51.470
Huh?

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.260
It looks like we're making major
sales at a particular store.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.260
That's his store!

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.240
Marimo Books

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:01.470
Now that I think about it,

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:06.390
this was the store with
good sales of my books last time

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.330
and the time before that, too.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.210
Why is that? The store's location?

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.390
Or the customer demographic there?

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.980
Well, whatever the reason is, I'm grateful.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:21.990
This means that he...

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:30.920
I guess he's also someone I'd consider
to be in that group of special people.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:35.160
It looks like life is going well for him...

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:40.660
Falling in love with him would be pointless.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.350
Don't even bother falling in love with him.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.170
I know, I know!

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.160
I really do know!

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.550
I'm an annoying customer
who doesn't buy anything,

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.230
just stands around and reads in the store.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.920
I'm here for this salesman.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.380
And he's a guy.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.470
This is bad.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.650
I'm basically stalking him!

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:09.210
I bet he would even recognize my face by now.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.370
Kisa.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.320
Mr. Yokozawa?!

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.720
What are you doing here?

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.820
Well, what are you doing here, sir?

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.350
I'm here for work.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:22.970
I'm here as a customer.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:27.570
God, he's the last person
I'd want to run into here!

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:30.800
He may be good at his job,
but he freaks me out!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.600
Have you ever talked to the
people who work at this store?

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.490
N-No!

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.950
Then come with me.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:41.740
Huh?

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:45.240
The book you're editing is
really selling here.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.780
It wouldn't hurt you to at least say hello.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.250
Uh, yes!

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:52.840
I guess he really keeps
track of these things.

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:57.430
Excuse me, but we're going to say
hello to the store manager, right?

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:58.880
Is there someone else you'd
like to say hello to?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.390
No! I'd like to talk to the manager.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.570
Hello.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.490
We work for Marukawa Publishing.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.970
Thank god.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.610
I'm totally not prepared
to talk to him right now.

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.150
Oh, hello!

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.650
Thank you so much for stopping by!

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:15.210
Is the manager here?

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:16.900
He's actually not in today.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:18.840
Then I guess you'll have to do.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.530
Hey, Mr. Yokozawa, what's
that supposed to mean?!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.670
That's so mean.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.450
He'll recognize my face, no doubt about it.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.190
Hey, where do you think you're going?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.810
This is the editor of Kana Morimoto's
manga that was released last week, Kisa.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.430
Hello.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:34.870
My name is Kisa.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:37.710
It's so nice to meet you.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.400
Shouta Kisa

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.420
G-God, this sucks.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.920
He knows for sure.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.430
It's nice to meet you, too.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:46.430
My name is Yukina. I'm in charge
of our store's shojo manga.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:50.310
What's up with our shelves?
They're so boring.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.070
That's not so.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.680
Can't you use more shelves over
there and make it pop more?

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:57.330
Of course.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:00.690
Of course he's not going to notice me.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:06.280
A store this large must get
hundreds of customers a day.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.430
So why do I feel vaguely disappointed?

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.040
I'm such an idiot.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.340
Mr. Yokozawa, can I see
you for just a moment?

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.430
Sure.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:24.870
Excuse me, but I have a meeting
now, so I'll be going.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.010
I don't actually, but whatever.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:29.310
I hope to see you again soon.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.210
Yes, me, too! Bye then!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.640
Why do I always do this?

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.630
I fall in love with someone,

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:42.230
then I get all of these ideas,

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.210
and then I feel brokenhearted.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.120
And it's always my fault.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.370
Shouta!

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:52.860
I've finally found you!

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:54.360
What are you doing here?

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:57.210
I'm here because I haven't
accepted that we broke up!

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.850
What are you talking about?
We were never going out.

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:01.710
How can you say that?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.470
Just shut up and keep your voice down!

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.610
Shouta!

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:09.540
We did it once. That doesn't
make me your boyfriend.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.600
Now fuck off!

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.730
You bastard!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:14.730
Sir,

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.000
is something wrong?

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.100
Wh-What the hell? Let me go!

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:23.450
I'm sorry, sir, but I can't have
you fighting inside our store.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:27.870
Hey, Shouta!

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.720
I doubt anyone would find me here.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.210
God, I can't believe that guy.

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:55.750
He still won't give up!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:03.270
I only went with him because
he was kind of my type.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:07.790
But ever since that day, he's been calling...

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:10.240
...and texting me every fifteen minutes!

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:15.250
I guess I only got what I deserved.

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:19.850
That's what you get for only
judging people by their looks.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:24.170
How do you ever expect to be in a
decent relationship with someone?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.260
Kou Yukina...

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.610
Now I finally know his name.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:37.270
Even his name has this
prince like air about it.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:40.770
I wonder if he overheard
what we were talking about?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.770
I'm sure he doesn't know anything
about things like that.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.450
Just let it go.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:49.800
I can't go back to that store after this.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.290
Oh, Mr. Kisa.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:15:00.220
I wouldn't have expected you to
know about this super obscure place.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:02.410
What the hell is he doing here?

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.150
Don't you have work?

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.840
My shift just ended.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:12.680
What about that guy at the store?

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:15.680
Oh, it seems he thought you were someone else.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.630
I was wondering about that!

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.530
It sure was a shock when
he suddenly grabbed my arm!

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:26.470
Did he really say that to him?

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:29.190
Or is he just saying that
now to me to be polite?

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.700
But didn't you have to be at a meeting?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:35.240
Oh, it was canceled actually.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.510
I'd like a coffee please.

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:38.810
Y-You're sitting down?

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:42.210
There's a lot of things I
want to talk to you about!

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.240
I knew it, he's loose.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:49.950
Kisa, is it possible that you were...

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:52.720
...Natsu Kihara and Yoko Mizushima's editor?

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:54.720
How do you know about that?

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:58.600
I was right?! I'm amazing!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.230
You know, their works aren't anything
alike, but they both have the same...

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.830
I don't know how to say
it. Atmosphere, I guess.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:05.730
The same atmosphere?

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.590
Hm, how should I put it?

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:13.200
Well, that's the impression I got, anyway.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:17.140
So you read shojo manga?

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:22.840
Of course! I've always liked this
fluffy, sparkly, love stuff,

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.790
but I would have never thought
they were edited by men.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:30.060
But I guess someone like you would
have no trouble with shojo manga.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.760
Are you mocking me?

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:33.760
Excuse me?

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:38.690
Anyway, it's amazing how far
you've gotten at your young age.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:39.350
Huh?

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:42.990
I mean, I figure we're around the same age.

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:46.270
I think it's really impressive that
you've produced works like those.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.690
May I ask how old you are?

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:53.780
I'm twenty-one and still going to university.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:55.780
I'm thirty.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:56.790
Huh?

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.780
I'm thirty years old.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:03.310
What?! No way! Really?!

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:05.670
Hang on, isn't there a limit to
how much younger you can look?!

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.290
Are you even trying to make sense?

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:12.300
W-Wow. I had no idea you
were that much older.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:14.950
Well, excuse me for being older.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:18.300
But this guy is way too young!

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:22.760
Oh crap, even without the gay angle,

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:25.310
I'm totally going into heartbreak territory.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.580
But you know,

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:31.320
being cute or looking younger
is like a gift you're born with.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:35.480
This guy is weird!

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:36.940
Here you go.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.570
Thank you.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:41.740
So, totally different topic,

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.740
but your new volume is really selling well!

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.880
I already put in an order
for an additional shipment.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.860
How many copies did you order?

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:48.540
Five hundred.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.560
That's too many!

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:51.730
It's fine.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:52.590
No, that's too many!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.590
Don't worry. I'll sell them all.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:05.600
If you say it like that, I
can't help but believe you.

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.230
You know, your store sells...

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:12.190
...about two to three times as
many of my books as the other stores.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.570
Yeah. Mr. Yokozawa said the same thing.

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:20.370
I wish the other stores sold
as many copies as yours does.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.630
Ignore what I just said!

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.870
Then our store will just have to sell
two to three times more than it does now.

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:28.950
Huh?

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.540
I mean, it doesn't matter where
the volumes are sold, right?

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.210
So long as they're sold?

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:35.530
I guess that's true.

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:37.380
We should have a fair!

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:41.390
If I pull an all nighter to make the display,

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.540
we can set it up tomorrow.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:45.580
You don't have to do that!

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:47.770
Something like that should be
discussed with the company...

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:51.410
I'm sure they'd have no problem
with some free advertising?

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:53.870
I always wanted to do
something like this anyway.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:58.470
Anyway, I'm an art student, so
I'm good at this kind of thing.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:01.030
Put this here...

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:02.760
Hey...

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.310
No really!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:08.840
I read the latest book first thing in
the morning, and it was really good.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.290
That's why I really want to promote it.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:15.600
I'm glad you feel that way, but
why are you doing all this?

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.800
Well, because it's your book.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:23.790
O-Oh, no. This is bad.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.660
This guy is experienced.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.310
Come on, I've got to open my eyes!

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:33.350
Why do I always allow myself
cling to these kind of false hopes?

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:44.150
This is bad...

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:47.330
I really love his face too much.

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.610
That's why these things
never work out for me.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.730
I fall for guys like this...

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:54.840
Kisa...

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:58.840
There are plenty of other
good looking guys out there.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.840
The last volume was really great.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:07.220
Don't tell anyone, but the
end really choked me up.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:08.700
The boss was like,

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.870
"What the hell are you crying
about so early in the morning?"

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:17.610
I really respect someone who can
make a book that touches you like that.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:21.340
I'm not the one who makes
them that way though.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:23.360
That's the authors...

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:29.620
But it's always the books you
edit that bring tears to my eyes.

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:33.140
Of course, I know that
the authors are amazing.

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:36.860
But I think that your work
is nothing to be disregarded.

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:41.130
What am I going to do?

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.730
This is really bad...

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:45.770
I want to touch him.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.720
I want to feel how warm he is.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.640
To feel what he feels like.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:57.650
Huh?

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:00.380
Damn, it's raining!

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:01.580
This sucks!

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:03.340
Do you have an umbrella?

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:06.740
If you don't, I can get
you an umbrella from here.

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:09.660
Kisa?

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:15.030
I'm just feeling this way because
he said something nice about me...

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.170
Of course this is also
just something fleeting...

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.150
Is something wrong?

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.490
Your face is red.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:25.980
Sorry, what?

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.370
I don't think...

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.470
...that I've ever really been
in love with anyone before.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.570
That's why I'm always thinking about this.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.190
What it would feel like...

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:43.650
...to really love someone?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:58.790
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:58.790
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:04.170
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:04.170
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:12.270
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:12.270
I fell in love with you

